            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jayanth Othayoth",
                        "email": "ojayanth@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ojayanth"
                    },
                    "message": "The issue with multi-cert PEM bundles creating untracked certificates is valid, but rejecting them outright in install() / replaceCertificate() is a breaking change.\nPEM bundles are commonly used (e.g., certificate chains), and current behavior already accepts them. Instead of strict rejection, consider:\n\nAccepting the bundle but using only the first cert\nLogging a warning for additional certificates\n\nIf rejection is required, it should be clearly documented as a behavior change. Also, limiting this to only authority and authorityBios seems ad-hoc\u2014worth evaluating consistency across types."
                }
            ],
